s"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/257754"} "35 from 22 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "At the 2007 World Championships, " [:a {:href "/athletes/103844"} "Valerie Vili"] " (NZL) outdueled Belarusian " [:a {:href "/athletes/103836"} "Nadezhda Ostapchuk"] ". They were back for Beijing and expected to repeat their battle. Also expected to contend was the 2006 European Champion, Ostapchuk’s teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/103853"} "Natalya Mikhnevich"] ". In the opening round, Vili struck first with 20.56 (67-5½), a new PR for her. And that would win the gold medal. Mikhnevich answered in round two with her best mark, 20.28 (66-6½), but that was only good for the silver. Ostapchuk struggled early and barely qualified for the final three throws. In round five, she got off 19.86 (65-2), good for the bronze medal. Vili did not quit after her opening winner, posting an excellent series with 20.40 (66-11¼) in round two, 20.26 (66-5¾) in round three, and 20.52 (67-4) in round five."] "\n\n" [:p {} "That was how the event and the results seemed to have ended. In 2015, however, the IOC began re-testing samples from the 2008 Beijing and 2012 London Olympics, using newer, more advanced testing techniques, in an effort to find those who had used performance enhancing drugs (PEDs), but in whom it could not be detected at the time of those Olympics. This was one of the many events affected."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The silver and bronze medals had initially gone to Belarussians Nataliya Mikhnevich and Nadezhda Ostapchuk, respectively. In November 2016 Khoronenko was disqualified for a positive re-test for methandienone and stanozolol, while in January 2017 Ostapchuk was disqualified for a positive re-test for turinabol (dehydrochloromethyltestosterone) and tamoxifen. The medals were re-assigned to " [:a {:href "/athletes/103850"} "Misleydis González"] " (CUB / silver) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/114781"} "Gong Lijiao"] " (CHN / bronze). Ostapchuk was also disqualified from the 2012 Olympics, testing positive during the Games, after seemingly winning a gold medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2545"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103844"} "Valerie Vili"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NZL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/NZL.png"}] "NZL"]] [:td {} "19.73 (1)"] [:td {} "20.56 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1467"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103850"} "Misleydis González"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CUB"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CUB.png"}] "CUB"]] [:td {} "18.91 (5)"] [:td {} "19.50 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1340"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/114781"} "Gong Lijiao"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "19.46 (2)"] [:td {} "19.20 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "2838"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/114782"} "Anna Omarova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} "18.74 (6)"] [:td {} "19.08 (4)"] [:td {}] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "5"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1907"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/82